{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויסתר משה פניו", :translit "vayaster moshe panav", :gloss "and Moses hid his face"} {:he "ויסתר עמל מעיני", :translit "vayaster amal me'einai", :gloss "and trouble would be hidden from my eyes"} {:he "עמו אנכי בצרה", :translit "imo anochi betzarah", :gloss "I am with him in distress"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויסתר משה פניו" "ויסתר עמל מעיני"]}], :frame {:text "The thornbush (sneh) symbolizes that God is with Israel in their oppression, derived from the phrase עמו אנכי בצרה, which is a permutation of אנכי בסנה (I am in the bush) — the same letters reordered (Shemot Rabbah 2:5). This midrashic reading establishes that the bush's lowly, thorny nature represents Israel suffering in Egyptian bondage, and that God's presence there signifies shared distress (Shemot Rabbah 2:5). The verse ויסתר עמל מעיני is from Psalms 10:11.", :sources ["Shemot Rabbah 2:5" "Psalms 10:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויסתר משה פניו" "ויסתר עמל מעיני"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויסתר משה פניו", :refs ["Exodus 3:6"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויסתר עמל מעיני", :refs ["Job 3:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:16.691538715Z", :model "glm-5.2"}